# access(1)

## NAME

access - show the owner and members of the computer, and request changes

## SYNOPSIS

    access
    access add NAME
    access remove NAME|UUID
    access transfer NAME

## DESCRIPTION

Without operands, prints the state (`unowned`, `owned` or `locked`), the owner, the members (name and UUID) and the invites (players added by name who have not used the computer yet).

`add`, `remove` and `transfer` only send a request. Nothing changes until the owner (or an operator) approves it in the game: the owner gets a chat message with Approve and Deny buttons while online. Run `access` again to see the result.

- `add NAME`: invite the player. They become a member when they next use the computer.
- `remove NAME|UUID`: remove a member by UUID, or an invite by name. With a name, an online member of that name is removed too.
- `transfer NAME`: make the online player NAME the owner. The old owner does not stay a member. On a computer without an owner, NAME must approve it.

Requests expire after a while, and only a few can wait at once. Repeating the same request does not send another message.

This is about players in the game, not files: programs on the computer are not separated by user.

## EXIT STATUS

0 when the request was sent. 1 when it was refused (`too many requests are waiting for approval`, `not supported on this computer`, `not a player name`). 2 for a usage error.

